WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.580
Say hello to the latest graduate of the Mighty
Marvel fitness program.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.900
Kumail Nanjiani recently took to Instagram
to post pics of himself after getting absolutely

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:16.309
shredded for his role in Marvel Studios' upcoming
epic The Eternals, and the entirety of the

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:19.099
internet promptly lost its mind.

00:00:19.099 --> 00:00:23.349
Nanjiani now rivals fellow funnyman Chris
Pratt for the most astonishing metamorphosis

00:00:23.349 --> 00:00:26.109
to be undergone for a Marvel film.

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:30.419
You'll recall that Pratt, who was best-known
for the role of the rather portly Andy Dwyer

00:00:30.419 --> 00:00:35.820
on the classic comedy series Parks and Recreation,
posted a similarly startling photo to Instagram

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:39.570
shortly before the release of 2014's Guardians
of the Galaxy.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:45.190
Nanjiani, who is probably most recognized
for his role on HBO's Silicon Valley, has

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:48.040
always been a somewhat skinny, gangly type.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.690
Now, he and Pratt have something else in common
besides their roles in Cosmic-based Marvel

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:58.560
films and being hilarious: they both look
like they've been sculpted from freaking marble.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:03.380
Nanjiani posted a long missive along with
the photos in which, to his credit, he acknowledged

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:07.319
that it's not just anybody who can hit the
gym and pull off such a transformation in

00:01:07.319 --> 00:01:09.979
such a seemingly short time.

00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:11.710
Nanjiani's caption read, in part,

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:16.639
"I never thought I'd be one of those people
who would post a thirsty shirtless, but I've

00:01:16.639 --> 00:01:20.759
worked way too hard for way too long so here
we are.

00:01:20.759 --> 00:01:25.140
You either die a hero, or you live long enough
to see yourself become the villain.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:30.149
I found out a year ago I was going to be in
Marvel's Eternals and decided I wanted to

00:01:30.149 --> 00:01:31.959
transform how I looked.

00:01:31.959 --> 00:01:36.340
I would not have been able to do this if I
didn't have a full year with the best trainers

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.270
and nutritionists paid for by the biggest
studio in the world.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:44.600
I'm glad I look like this, but I also understand
why I never did before.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:48.529
It would have been impossible without these
resources and time."

00:01:48.529 --> 00:01:53.149
He went on to thank the trainers who, quote,
"made [him] understand true physical pain

00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:58.869
for months and months," and deadpanned, "I
think I can almost touch my toes now."

00:01:58.869 --> 00:02:04.009
Nanjiani's wife, writer and producer Emily
V. Gordon, responded to a cheeky "congratulations"

00:02:04.009 --> 00:02:05.369
comment on Twitter, saying,

00:02:05.369 --> 00:02:10.390
"My husband works hard for every role he takes,
but he's worked hard in many new ways for

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:11.390
this one.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:12.840
I'm so proud of him.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.130
I always have been.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:19.510
Also, we spent the majority of this past weekend
playing Borderlands 3 so don't think he's

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:20.990
changed too much."

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:25.370
Nanjiani will be taking on one of the more
interesting roles among The Eternals' enormous

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:32.110
ensemble cast: that of Kingo Sunen, who settled
down in Japan centuries ago, isolating himself

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:35.570
from his fellow Eternals and learning the
ways of the samurai.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:40.730
He typically wields a nigh-unbreakable sword
that can cut through virtually any material,

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:44.520
but this is the only advantage he tends to
deem acceptable.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:49.870
While he possesses the powers inherent to
all Eternals - flight, super strength, energy

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:55.610
projection, near-immortality - he normally
refuses to use said powers in combat, preferring

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.440
to fight in the traditional manner of the
samurai.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:03.070
In the comics, he uses these skills in the
modern age to become a world-famous movie

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:07.740
star, usually portraying samurai and martial
artists in Japanese action films.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:12.510
If you ask us, it's this quirk that makes
Nanjiani perfect for the role; you can just

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:17.100
picture him going on about honor and tradition
before donning sunglasses and speeding away

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:22.050
in some ridiculously rare sports car, so as
not to be late for the day's shoot.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:27.780
We have no doubt that Nanjiani will be a standout
among The Eternals' cast, the largest ensemble

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.270
Marvel has ever fielded for a non-team-up
movie.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:35.090
Obviously, this flick is shaping up to be
a Marvel adventure quite unlike any we've

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.310
seen before, and it's sure to impress.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:39.610
"Do you like movies?"

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.810
"Depends on the movie."

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:43.900
"I'm the exact same way."

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:48.410
Owing to the timeless nature of its heroes,
Marvel boss Kevin Feige has said that it may

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:52.730
very well be an epic that spans "tens of thousands
of years."

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:57.460
One thing we can say for sure, however: Kumail
Nanjiani will be looking damn good while cracking

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.810
wise and slashing foes to ribbons.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:04.150
The Eternals hits the big screen on November
6th, 2020.

